    "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #16. Centralises every provider connection on a new **Settings → Connections** nav surface and replaces the broken legacy \"Try directly\" probes (which fired URLs like `https://api.telegram.org/bot/getMe` with no token and 404'd every time) with template-driven URLs built from real, persisted credentials.\n\n### What changed\n\n- **New Settings view** (`js/src/web/settings-view.js`) — single nav surface with one card per provider. Each card has typed credential inputs (token / app id / phone number id / etc.), Save and Forget buttons, an archive **file upload + paste-fallback** textarea, and a Try-directly probe.\n- **Probe URLs are template-derived** (`probeUrlTemplate` per provider in `connection-guides.js` → `buildProbeUrl()`). Templates interpolate `{token}`, `{appId}`, `{phoneNumberId}`, etc. from saved credentials. If any required field is missing the probe button stays disabled — no more 404/400 round-trips.\n- **Per-section \"Connect first\" CTA** (`SettingsConnectFirstCta`) — every empty-state section (Chat, Comms, Hiring, …) now has a button that deep-links into Settings → Connections and scrolls to the matching provider card via the existing `meta-sovereign:navigate` CustomEvent.\n- **Credentials encrypted at rest** — `secret:*` links are persisted via the existing `wrapSecretStore` (AES-256-GCM, derived from `secretPassphrase`). The integration test asserts the on-disk `data.lino` contains ciphertext, never the plaintext token.\n- **Secrets stay local** — `secret:*` links are filtered from outbound and inbound peer sync (existing behaviour, verified by the new tests).\n- **Case study** at `docs/case-studies/issue-16/` documents the bug, root cause, requirements (R-O1..R-O19), solution plan, components touched, and external research. Includes before/after screenshots.\n- **REQUIREMENTS.md** — new Section O (R-O1..R-O19) with traceability to source files and tests.\n\n### Test coverage\n\n- `js/tests/connection-guides-templates.test.js` — unit tests for `buildProbeUrl()` template interpolation, missing-field handling, and `credentialsFromLinks()`.\n- `js/tests/settings-credentials-roundtrip.test.js` — integration test that boots a real `startServer` with `secretPassphrase`, PUTs a `secret:telegram:bot-token` via `/links`, reads it back, recovers credentials via `credentialsFromLinks()`, builds the probe URL, and asserts:\n  - URL is `https://api.telegram.org/bot{token}/getMe` (with token), never the broken legacy `…/bot/getMe`.\n  - On-disk `data.lino` contains ciphertext, never plaintext.\n  - DELETE clears the credential and `buildProbeUrl()` returns `null` (R-O2).\n- `js/tests/e2e-browser-spa.mjs` — new `stepSettingsCredentialRoundtrip` step drives the real SPA in Playwright: types a token into Settings → Connections → Telegram, saves, asserts the probe button is enabled, then verifies the chat-empty Connect-first CTA navigates back to Settings with `#conn-telegram` hash.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` — all 219 tests pass\n- [x] `npm run lint` — clean\n- [x] `npm run format:check` — clean\n- [x] `npm run build:web` — bundle rebuilt (`js/src/web/app.min.js`)\n- [x] Pre-commit hooks (lint-staged) pass\n- [ ] CI green on `416fdc6`\n- [ ] Manual smoke: open Settings → Connections, paste a Telegram bot token, click \"Try directly\", confirm 200 OK from `api.telegram.org`\n\n## Files of note\n\n- `js/src/web/connection-guides.js` — provider catalogue + `buildProbeUrl` + `credentialsFromLinks`\n- `js/src/web/settings-view.js` — new Settings nav surface\n- `js/src/web/connection-guide.js` — per-section Connect-first CTA\n- `js/tests/settings-credentials-roundtrip.test.js` — integration test\n- `js/tests/connection-guides-templates.test.js` — unit tests\n- `js/tests/e2e-browser-spa.mjs` — e2e step\n- `docs/case-studies/issue-16/` — full case study\n- `docs/REQUIREMENTS.md` — Section O (R-O1..R-O19)\n- `.changeset/issue-16-provider-connections.md` — changeset for next release\n\n## Screenshots\n\nBefore/after captures of the Settings surface and the working Telegram probe live at `docs/case-studies/issue-16/screenshot1.png` and `screenshot2.png`.\n",
